Created `Services/FileSystemWrapper.cs` — a delegating wrapper that implements `IFileSystem` by forwarding all members to an inner instance. All properties are `virtual`, so you can subclass it and override only the parts you need:

```csharp
public class LoggingFileSystem(IFileSystem inner, ILogger logger) 
    : FileSystemWrapper(inner)
{
    public override IFile File => // wrap with logging
}
```

This keeps your production code using `IFileSystem` unchanged while letting you layer in behavior via decoration.
